From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:09:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Nintendo DS build

Makefile.nds builds a DSi enhanced .nds with the toolchain of the ports
(clang, calico and libnds), with int sized enums like Quake expects and
common symbols for the globals it defines in headers. The collision code
and compiler-rt's software floating point, which Quake uses everywhere as
the ARM9 has no floating point unit, run from ITCM as ARM code: the
floating point objects are taken out of compiler-rt and renamed for ITCM,
they are linked before it. Constants are single precision, so expressions
like x * 0.5 don't go through double precision. HOT_CODE puts single
functions in ITCM, the rest is Thumb code in main RAM: the QuakeC
interpreter, BoxOnPlaneSide, Mod_PointInLeaf, RecursiveLightPoint and
R_DrawParticles. The float comparisons come from fcmp_nds.s instead of
compiler-rt, whose comparisons take two calls.
